    "input": "{\"current_utc\": \"2026-09-24T17:15:41.968427+00:00\", \"assigned_topic\": {\"study_topic_id\": \"study-b648bf27885bad80a79e\", \"subject_id\": \"subject-d0aef339b597496f04f5\", \"topic\": \"Francisco Goya\", \"primary_category\": \"Arts and Music\", \"description\": \"Spanish painter and printmaker whose works include the Black Paintings, Los Caprichos, The Disasters of War, and The Third of May 1808.\", \"subcategory_ids\": [\"arts-001\", \"arts-003\", \"arts-010\"], \"level_occurrence_counts\": {\"high-school\": 1, \"middle-school\": 1}, \"role_occurrence_counts\": {\"answer\": 2}, \"source_question_count\": 2, \"aliases\": [\"Francisco José de Goya y Lucientes\", \"Francisco de Goya\", \"Goya\"], \"topic_type\": \"person\", \"source_ids\": [\"qb-0606b2302077a769dab92f2f\", \"qb-b8f10056ab76644e69889629\"], \"source_questions\": [{\"custom_id\": \"qb-0606b2302077a769dab92f2f\", \"level\": \"high-school\", \"question_type\": \"bonuses\", \"source\": \"2022 SHOW-ME\", \"round\": \"14\", \"number\": \"16\", \"parts\": [{\"label\": \"L\", \"question\": \"This series includes a painting in which two men trapped knee-deep in sand battle with weapons called Fight with Cudgels. For 10 points each:\", \"answer\": \"\"}, {\"label\": \"A\", \"question\": \"[H] Name this series of pieces painted directly onto the walls of the artist’s house, the Quinta del Sordo. Another piece in this series, Witches’ Sabbath, depicts Satan in the form of a goat.\", \"answer\": \"Black Paintings\"}, {\"label\": \"B\", \"question\": \"[M] This deaf Spanish artist included Saturn Devouring His Son in his Black Paintings.\", \"answer\": \"Francisco Goya [or Francisco José de Goya y Lucientes]\"}, {\"label\": \"C\", \"question\": \"[E] Goya’s The Disasters of War series protests this leader’s invasion of Spain during the Peninsular War. In a Jacques-Louis David painting, this French emperor is depicted crossing the Alps.\", \"answer\": \"Napoleon Bonaparte [accept Napoleon I]\"}]}, {\"custom_id\": \"qb-b8f10056ab76644e69889629\", \"level\": \"middle-school\", \"question_type\": \"bonuses\", \"source\": \"2020 ERIS\", \"round\": \"8\", \"number\": \"17\", \"parts\": [{\"label\": \"L\", \"question\": \"Answer the following about fine art and popular music, for 10 points each:\", \"answer\": \"\"}, {\"label\": \"A\", \"question\": \"[10] A 2016 album by Swedish djent band Meshuggah is titled The Violent Sleep of Reason, a reference to this Spanish artist's The Sleep of Reason Produces Monsters, one of his Los Caprichos etchings. He also painted The Third of May, 1808.\", \"answer\": \"Francisco [José de] Goya [y Lucientes]\"}, {\"label\": \"B\", \"question\": \"[10] This American musical artist sang \\\"And how you suffered for your sanity / And how you tried to set them free\\\" in \\\"Vincent\\\", a song addressed to Vincent van Gogh. He is better known for singing about \\\"the day the music died\\\" in \\\"American Pie\\\".\", \"answer\": \"Don McLean\"}, {\"label\": \"C\", \"question\": \"[10] The pioneering pop artist Richard Hamilton designed the album cover for this band's \\\"White Album\\\". John Lennon and Paul McCartney were both members of this rock band from Liverpool.\", \"answer\": \"The Beatles\"}]}]}}",
